    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe mobile keyboard can cover the food quantity field, and typed fractional amounts may not persist, leaving coarse stepper buttons as the usable fallback. This is the [directly requested scope-only investigation](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/issues/405#issuecomment-6049387731). Source inspection found intended decimal support and prior fixes in merged PR343, but did not reproduce the reported failure.\n\n## Requirements and acceptance\n\n- Keep the focused amount and save action reachable while the keyboard is open.\n- Preserve valid typed values such as 0.125, 1.3 and supported comma decimals through dismissal, immediate save, reopening and reload. Do not snap typed values to button increments.\n- Preserve supported precision, serving-unit conversion and corresponding calorie calculations.\n- Invalid or empty values show validation rather than silently restoring or saving another amount.\n- Offline save/replay and retries retain the intended quantity without duplicate entries.\n- Cover add-food and existing-log correction; assess Saved foods/recipe controls only where shared behavior is affected. Native-device execution remains explicitly deferred for review readiness.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\nA read-only source investigation found NumberStepperField preserves text and accepts comma decimals; getFoodQuantityStep controls button increments. Add-food uses FoodSelectionEditor inside KeyboardAwareScrollView with enclosing Android height/iOS padding avoidance. Existing-log edits convert displayed amounts into servings before online submission or offline queuing.\n\nBefore proposing a correction, reproduce against the exact current build and trace draft/focus/keyboard events, immediate-save ordering, FoodLogContent dirty detection, payload construction, response and outbox replay. Inspect modal height constraints and native focus-handle behavior. Return the smallest demonstrated fix and interaction/persistence regression plan. Genuine matched browser evidence may support applicable changes, but simulated keyboard behavior must not be described as device proof.\n\nThis issue records scoping only; implementation and PR publication have not been admitted.\n\n## Implementing Codex task\n\nScoping completed in verified task `01a11c77-0cff-76e7-b21f-6f5702949026`. Implementation is unassigned.\n\n## Implementing PR\n\nNot created.\n",
